Wait, `MemoryProviderProfileStore.save(definition, -1)`. And then GET profile → PUT it back verbatim.

The test needs to assert:
- PUT returns 200
- the re-read projection matches (idempotent round-trip): compare all fields but revision.

Also a case with reasoning/cache capabilities set (so the round trip covers non-empty reasoning levels and full vocabulary), e.g. a second profile with capabilities [TEXT, REASONING, PROMPT_CACHE, STREAMING, TOOL_CALL, USAGE, IMAGE_INPUT], reasoning levels [LOW, HIGH, XHIGH], maxBudget 4096, cache supported+longRetention.

The round trip must be "GET 投影 → 原样 PUT 回写" — the body is the projection plus expectedRevision. To be faithful to the UI, I should build the body as `body = projection; body.expectedRevision = revision`. In Java with Jackson, I can do: read the GET response into an ObjectNode, put "expectedRevision", and serialize. That's precisely "原样写回" and avoids hand-writing the payload.

