```java
@Test
void providerProfileRestAcceptsItsOwnProjectionUnchanged() throws Exception {
    ... setup with two profiles: "openai-default" (unconfigured shape) and "faux-configured" (rich shape)
    for (String profileId : List.of("openai-default", "faux-configured")) {
        JsonNode projection = json(GET /api/v1/provider-profiles/{id});
        ObjectNode echo = (ObjectNode) projection.deepCopy();
        echo.put("expectedRevision", projection.path("revision").asLong());
        HttpResponse<String> saved = PUT ... mapper.writeValueAsString(echo)
        assertEquals(200, saved.statusCode(), saved.body());
        JsonNode replayed = json(saved);
        // everything except revision round-trips unchanged
        ObjectNode expected = (ObjectNode) projection.deepCopy();
        expected.put("revision", replayed.path("revision").asLong());
        assertEquals(expected, replayed);
    }
}
```

That's a strong assertion: projection identity across a write.

Wait — careful: does `providerProfile` projection include all fields? Yes: profileId, revision, family, baseUrl, credential, headerCredentials, models, defaultModel, settings. And the PUT body may contain extra keys (profileId, revision) — the parser ignores unknown keys (it reads only known ones). Fine.

